# Float Test
# Carbon (C) — real density 2.267 g/cm³. Archimedes decides: ρ vs 0.997 g/cm³.
scene "Carbon Float Test"

floater = cube 20mm material: carbon at (0, 60mm, 0)
pool = cube(w: 90mm, d: 90mm, h: 35mm) material: water at (0, 17.5mm, 0)
# real verdict for Carbon: sinks (density 2.267 g/cm³)
ask "will it float?"
simulate: float
